────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WEB SOURCE NATURE (faithful-parity note)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
`web/src/components/layout/sidebar/NotionSidebar.tsx` is a PRESENTATIONAL component — it fetches NOTHING.
It shares the EXACT data contract with its sibling LinearSidebar (the web imports
`LinearSidebarSectionInput as NotionSidebarSectionInput` + `LinearSidebarProps as NotionSidebarProps`). Its
hooks are `useTranslation` (P1/S10) + `useLocation` (router pathname); the nav tree + pinned list + badge
counts arrive as PROPS from Layout, and pin/unpin/navigation route OUT via callbacks. It therefore has NO
loading/error/stale/offline data-state branches — inventing them would contradict the source (Covenant 5).

Its REAL render branches (all reproduced natively):
  • Favorites group present (≥1 pinned) vs. absent.                    • The permanent "Pages" group label.
  • Section collapsed vs. expanded (caret rotates).                    • Section glyph = first item's icon.
  • Active row = quiet bg fill ONLY (NO accent bar, NO bold weight).   • Trailing badge: dot / chip / none.
  • EVERY row carries a pin(star)/unpin(close) affordance.            • Inline tree-filter active vs. inactive.
  • Empty-filter branch ("No matches." + "Clear filter").            • No-data → friendly empty (native P4).

Notion vs. Linear parity differences faithfully encoded:
  • New i18n key `nav.pages` = "Pages" (permanent, always-shown group label).
  • `nav.pinPage` = "Pin {{page}}" (NOT "...to favorites" — that is Linear's string).
  • An ALREADY-PINNED section row resolves to UNPIN (web `pinAction` close button), never "no affordance"
    (Linear returns null there). Verified by testAlreadyPinnedSectionRowResolvesToUnpinNotNone.
  • Section header is one quiet clickable line: caret + glyph + sentence-case title + count (not uppercase).

